Am 30.07.2014 04:49, schrieb Matthew Ward:
> I'm playing a wizard and got a pretty good start. Now I'm pretty sure
> I'll die, because I got one of those Big Rooms that contain the
> stairs to Sokoban.

Bigroom is no fatal disease; no reason to die. :-)

WRT stairs to Sokoban; you may engrave the E-word (assuming not too
many humanoids interfering) and wait until all monsters are close to
the stairs, then climb the stairs and dig down; you may land in an
area close to the Sokoban stairs, or close to the downstairs (to
continue exploration), or in an empty area where you can continue
digging and dungeon exploration below Bigroom. Sokoban may have a
wand of fire or lightning for a permanent engraving of the E-word.

> It feels too early to survive. What do people do in this situation?

Stay on the stairs. Engrave Elbereth. Melee only when not surrounded
by monsters because dust engravongs will instantly get erased. Take
special cares of humanoids (like elves) which don't respect Elbereth.
If you have wands of fire or lightning burn the E-word and fight until
nothing moves any more.

As you are a wizard you may have some offensive spells, or sleep? Use
those spells, fight and retreat upstairs if necessary to heal HP and
restore PW. (Don't forget that you will need a lot more food.)

>
> My thoughts:
>
> 1. Try to get AC protection in mine town (the altar is aligned), but
> this is rough because I've leveled up to 8 already, so I could do
> this at most once and that once is unsure.

Then try to get better (mithril-) armor from the mines' inhabitants.
(But note that you may not any more be able to cast spells reliably,
as suggested above as another option.)

A minetown tool shop may have some horn or drum to scare monsters.
In certain minetowns you can find spellbooks that may help you to
clear the Bigroom. (Be aware that if you buy 2-4 AC protection from
your money may make it impossible to buy helpful items then! - Do
you have a pet to steal items for you?)

A polytrap in minetown can make your pet a killer that can clear
Bigromm alone, while you wait and observe the massacre. If you don't
have a pet any more then get one.

>
> 2. Quaff fountains in hopes of a wish (I know, this is a bad idea).

Yes, this is probably a bad idea since you have a lot other options
still available.

>
> Notes: I have no means of polypiling. Defense: cloak of magic
> resistance, studded leather armor, and iron skull cap, all +0, so AC
> 5. Attack: blessed +1 quarterstaff skilled up to advanced and force
> bolt. I have a lot of unidentified scrolls, a few unidentified rings,
> and no potions.

The rings may contain some types with hard gems; you can apply those
to create tactical semi-permanent E-word engravings. (Mind that you
will need one turn per letter, and the engraving may get erased when
moving.) Hard gems to engrave can also be found in the mines, if not
early then on mines-end level.

>
> It feels like this should not be the end for any reasonable player.

You have options.

Also, while resting on an E-square, take care of missiles and wands
used by some of the monsters.

Also mind, that even if you avoid Bigroom for now the mines may be
deadly as well; quite open area.

Also try to sacrifice for your artifact weapon; wizards get Magicbane
that will provide you with a means to semi-perma engrave in 1 turn!
(Very helpful, specifically in Bigroom.) If you've not yet seen an
altar, see whether minetown's temple is co-aligned.

